  "rationale": "Attendees {u1..u4}; u5 is not coming but submitted a pair vote. Phase 1: m1 rows u1,u2,u3 yes / u4 no -> attendee_votes 4, coverage 1.00, yes 3, approval 3/4 = 0.75. m2 rows u1,u2 yes / u3,u4 no -> attendee_votes 4, coverage 1.00, yes 2, approval 2/4 = 0.50 (exactly at the floor, passes). Finalists ranked by yes-votes: m1 (3), m2 (2). Runoff, attendees only: m1 preferred by u3,u4 = 2; m2 preferred by u1,u2 = 2 -> 2-2, neither wins strictly more, so the pair has no winner. Copeland: m1 = 0, m2 = 0 -> tie, no Condorcet winner. Rung 2, approval: m1 0.75 > m2 0.50 -> m1 wins. Counting u5's vote for m2 would make it 3-2 for m2 and produce a Condorcet winner m2 instead.",
